WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
[intro music]

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.920
Good morning, Hank. It's Friday, July 27th, and I have really exciting news!

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.960
That might have been too much it's not that exciting. I have reasonably exciting news.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.920
Actually, after the excitement of the last couple days, that's probably even too much.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.360
I have news that I find exciting that you probably won't.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.760
That's right, I finished cataloging my home library. YES!

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.680
This is something I've wanted to do ever since we left New York, when I had to pack up all those books I said to myself,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:40.960
"When we move, I am going to make a brilliantly catalogued library so that I will never lose another book again in my entire life."

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:47.600
And now with the help of librarything.com and the New York Public Library's Guide to Organizing a Home Library in your pants, I've done it!

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.060
That's right, I own a book about how to organize your library.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.760
This is off-topic, but I wonder exactly how many books can fit inside the library in my pants.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:01.280
I know that right now the flamers are all like flexing their little flame fingers, preparing to write, "YOU ARE A NERD"

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.420
Hank, I have a serious question: why is being a nerd bad? Saying I noticed you're a nerd is like saying, "

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.580
"Hey I noticed that you'd rather be intelligent than be stupid, that you'd rather be thoughtful than be vapid,

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.320
that you believe that there are things that matter more than the arrest record of Lindsay Lohan.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.320
Why is that?"

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:19.380
In fact, it seems to me that most contemporary insults are pretty lame.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.780
Even lame is kind of lame.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.240
Saying you're lame is like saying, "you walk with a limp."

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.900
Yeah, whatever, so does 50 Cent.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.060
He's done alright for himself.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:30.480
It's not that I mind being insulted, it's that I mind being insulted so poorly.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.940
There are plenty of great insults, I mean, you could be like,

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.560
"You are way too focused on yourself."

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.880
You want to talk about some insults? Let's talk about Shakespeare's insults

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.800
I mean here's a conversation of contemporary insults:

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:43.625
You're a dork.

00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:44.425
You're a geek.

00:01:44.425 --> 00:01:45.320
You suck.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.400
No, you suck.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.680
Compare that with the conversation made out of real Shakespearean insults:

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.100
I think that you're a herd of boils and plagues.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.420
You monstrous malefactor.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.160
Mad headed puke-stocking

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.720
You stuffed cloak bag of guts.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.200
You're just a huge bombard of sack.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.040
You barren-spoiled man.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.860
You carcass fit for hounds.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.100
Dude, "carcass fit for hounds"? That's a burn.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.120
Yeah I know right?

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.040
"Carcass fit for hounds" - not bad!

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.760
You valuet flea, you foul and ugly witch.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.400
Oh shut up, you presumptuous vassal.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.760
You fat and greasy citizen, you saucy lackey. You fancy-mongerer.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.340
Oh, yeah, well you're a mildewed ear.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.760
You're a timorous wrench.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.720
Maybe so but you're a foul misshapen stigmatic with an odiferous stench.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.520
You foul undigested lump.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.541
Wait, lump of what?

00:02:31.541 --> 00:02:34.680
Shakespeare didn't specify. Maybe like big league chew.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.080
That's disgusting, I'm just like a pound of big league chew sitting in somebody's stomach.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:42.100
Now, that's how you insult people with Shakespeare.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.640
Nerdfighters for the win.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.940
Hank, I'll see you on Monday.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:50.660
Oh wait - I forgot to show you my home library! HOORAY HOME LIBRARY.

